# Role: creative but **shippable** residual ideas — **no product code** this pass
# Audience: Domain Experts (implement winner) · peers (smoke / FP-FN) · Memory
# Scope: `c_guard_scan_idents` 7.1 close — **not** M1–M20, not full IFC

## Problem (tree truth)

| Fact | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| Sprint pin | `SPRINT.oot` 7.1 CRIT: `c_guard_scan_idents` **stack buffer** (no per-char OoStr leak) |
| Wording is stale | `.oo` has **no** C stack `char[]`. Memory lane already said: 7.1 style = **one `str_slice` per ident span**, not a C buffer (`audit/t1_memory.oot`) |
| Walker exists | `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo` `c_guard_scan_idents` — linear C-arg walk; skip `"..."` + `\\`; skip `//` and `/* */`; ident = `_`/alpha start, alnum/`_` cont; **one** `str_slice(args, start, i)` then `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` |
| Call site | `c_secret_emit_guard` after a0/a1/a2 — full `args` scan on sealed sinks (println family, write_file, fetch, sys_exec, env/OS, net, FFI) |
| Dual path already | Check/emit token walk: `c_secret_scan_call` on lexer **IDENT** (`c_emit_secret.oo`). Emit-lower C-text walk: `c_guard_scan_idents` on joined arg string (`c_emit_lower.oo` / `c_emit_call.oo`) |
| 7.2 sibling | `c_sys_exec_last_arg` already **one** `str_slice(args, last_start, n)` (`c_emit_args.oo`). Same SPRINT CRIT class; same “prove/close?” handoff |
| 7.10 still leaks | `c_parse_secret_env` still `name = name + c` per ident char (`c_emit_secret.oo:60`) — HIGH, same slice pattern |
| Shared state machines | String/escape skip copied in `c_guard_scan_idents`, `c_sys_exec_last_arg`, `c_count_top_args`. Alpha-class oracles copied in 7.1 + 7.10 |
| Handoff | `audit/shutdown_handoff_2026-08-12_r2_swarm.oot`: 7.1 “source comments claim str_slice already; **needs prove/close only?**” |
| T2 security already probed | `audit/t2_security.oot`: string/comment FP = 0 on product host; real IDENT refuse dual-path. **Fixtures exist** under `ooda/fixtures/secret_t2_*.oo` |
| T2 smoke gap | `scripts/secret_t2_depth_smoke.sh` does **not** wire `secret_t2_string_*` / `secret_t2_comment_*` (field/method/multi-arg/midline only) |
| Alias rail | Token + resolve: `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` / `__alias__`. Fixtures: `secret_alias_rebind_{pass,fail}.oo`, `secret_t1_alias_println.oo`. T1 smoke owns rebind; 7.1 smoke should not re-own sticky-clear |

**Not this wave:** full IFC, AST multi-arg lattice, `${}` interp (5.8), macro-body second pass (2.8), replacing emit with a new IR.

## Constraints (hard)

1. **Path A only** — fail-closed ident scan residual, not “perfect taint.”
2. **Do not greenwash 7.1 from comments.** Close only on **static slice proof + immune smoke**.
3. **Keep dual-path honesty.** Token IDENT walk (check) and C-text belt (emit args) disagree on some edges; deleting one without prove is FN risk.
4. **SPRINT “stack buffer” is not implementable in `.oo`.** Do not emit C `char buf[N]` from product `.oo` as the 7.1 fix.
5. **Reuse fixtures.** Prefer wiring `secret_t2_*` + alias rails over new theater files.
6. **Line pressure** — no new monofile; helper ≤ small file or existing `c_emit_args.oo` / `c_emit_secret.oo`.
7. **Fairy writes ideas only** — DE owns land + prove.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)

Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves 7.1 CRIT (heap thrash / missing body / unproved scan) |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no “stack buffer shipped”; no token/C-text lie |
| **Smoke** | Cheap pass+fail: string FP, comment FP, real IDENT, alias resolve |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (untested 7.1 FIXED, dual-scan drift, concat copies) |
| **Ship** | ≤ few small edits + smoke; uses existing walker / fixtures |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

