## Ideas evaluated

### I1 — Prove/close 7.1 as **already sliced** (no walker rewrite) ⭐
**Shape:** Treat 7.1 product code as landed (`str_slice` per span; no `name = name + c` in the walker). Close the CRIT with:
1. Static grep: `c_guard_scan_idents` contains `str_slice`; **no** ident concat in that fn.
2. Immune smoke (I5) on string / comment / real IDENT / alias-resolved refuse.
3. Rewrite SPRINT 7.1 line from “stack buffer” → **FIXED path-A (slice + prove)** or drop to residual note.
4. Named residual: C-text scan is still a **re-lexer** of lowered args, not token-stream (I2 later).

**Smoke:** I5 matrix.  
**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 9 · Entropy 9 · Ship 10 → **avg 9.4**  
**Why winner-class:** Handoff already asked “prove/close only?” Tree matches. Avoids thrash rewrite of a working belt.

### I2 — Replace C-text scan with **token-stream** only
**Shape:** Delete (or never call) `c_guard_scan_idents`. Rely solely on `c_secret_scan_call` / println IDENT walk over lexer toks. Strings/comments never become IDENT → FP class dissolves by construction.

**Smoke:** same T2 matrix; plus a case where lowered C text contains an ident that **tokens already classified** (must still refuse).  
**Darwin:** Close 5 · Honest 6 · Smoke 6 · Entropy 4 · Ship 4 → **avg 5.0**  
**Why weak now:** Emit guard runs on **joined C arg text** after `c_emit_call_args` (`c_emit_lower.oo`) — toks are not in that helper’s contract. Dropping C-text without passing toks is an **FN hole** on any sink that only the emit belt covers (full `args` after a0/a1/a2). Dual-path is the Path-A floor (`SECRET_TAINT.oot` §4–5).  
**Later:** only after emit-guard is wired to the same tok cursor as check (I3).

### I3 — Token-stream **at emit** (pass toks into `c_secret_emit_guard`)
**Shape:** Change `c_secret_emit_guard` / call sites to take `toks + start/end` of the arg list; walk IDENT the same as `c_secret_scan_call`. C-text scan becomes optional belt or dies.

**Darwin:** Close 7 · Honest 8 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 5 · Ship 2 → **avg 5.4**  
**Why later:** Signature change across `c_emit_lower` / `c_emit_call` / LLVM sibling. Architecture-adjacent. Does **not** fix 7.1 heap (already sliced). Correct long-term DRY vs dual re-lexers — **not this CRIT turn.**

### I4 — Shared **ident-slice** helper for 7.1 / 7.2 / 7.10 ⭐
**Shape:** One tiny helper (name e.g. `c_slice_ident_at(src, start) -> String` or `c_ident_end(src, start) -> Int` + caller `str_slice`):
- Start/cont class **once** (kill the 70-line `is_start`/`is_cont`/`is_al` copies).
- 7.1: `name = c_slice_ident_at(args, start)` (behavior-identical).
- 7.2: last-arg is a **comma span**, not an ident — helper does **not** rewrite last-arg (already sliced). Optional: share **string-skip** step only (`c_skip_c_string`) with `c_sys_exec_last_arg` / `c_count_top_args`.
- 7.10: replace `name = name + c` with `name = str_slice(src, name_start, k)` — **this is the remaining leak.**

**Minimal path-A:** helper in `c_emit_secret.oo` or `c_emit_args.oo` (already imported). No new package.

**Smoke:** 7.1 matrix (I5) + existing `secret_midline_safe` + one `// SECRET: longish_name` still tags; invalid empty name still `ERR secret`.  
**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 9 · Smoke 8 · Entropy 9 · Ship 8 → **avg 8.4**  
**Why ship-with-winner:** 7.1 itself is already slice-correct; helper **closes 7.10** with the 7.1 pattern and prevents the next agent from “fixing” 7.1 via concat or a fake C buffer.

### I5 — Smoke matrix: string / comment / alias (7.1 prove rail) ⭐
**Shape:** One small script (new `secret_s71_ident_scan_smoke.sh` **or** extend `secret_t2_depth_smoke.sh` — prefer **extend** to avoid dual truth). Dual-path `emit-c` + `check` where cheap.

| Case | Fixture (exists unless noted) | Expect |
|------|-------------------------------|--------|
| String FP bind | `secret_t2_string_fp.oo` | ALLOW (no `ERR secret`) |
| String lit arg FP | `secret_t2_string_lit_arg_fp.oo` | ALLOW |
| Substring spelling FP | `secret_t2_string_contains_name_fp.oo` | ALLOW |
| `//` comment FP | `secret_t2_comment_fp.oo` | ALLOW |
| Doc / blockish comment FP | `secret_t2_comment_blockish_fp.oo` | ALLOW |
| Mid-line `// SECRET:` | `secret_midline_safe.oo` (already in T2 smoke) | ALLOW |
| Real bare IDENT | `secret_t2_real_arg_fail.oo` / `secret_sink_fail.oo` | REFUSE |
| Multi-arg full scan | `secret_multi_arg_println_fail.oo` (already in T2) | REFUSE |
| Alias dest taint | `secret_alias_rebind_pass.oo` | REFUSE (`y` after `y = api_key`) |
| Alias sink name | `secret_t1_alias_println.oo` (`let f = println; f(secret)`) | REFUSE **or named residual** if Path-A only tracks IDENT→IDENT data alias, not callee alias on every emit path — **do not soft-OK** |
| Static 7.1 | grep walker | `str_slice` present; no per-char ident concat in `c_guard_scan_idents` |

**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6** (rails; not a solo product rewrite)  
**Why must-bundle:** Without this, “7.1 FIXED” is comment-greenwash (Zero Trust Agency). Fixtures are **already on disk** from T2 security — wire them.

### I6 — Literal SPRINT: C stack buffer in emit / runtime
**Shape:** Lower walker to C `char buf[64]` / `oodac` helper in `chs_rt`.  
**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 1 · Smoke 2 · Entropy 0 · Ship 1 → **avg 1.4 — DISQUALIFIED**  
**Why dies:** Wrong language layer; new FFI surface; SPRINT words are a **memory-class hint**, not a C ABI. `t1_memory.oot` already rejected this.

### I7 — Full AST / IFC multi-arg lattice (drop string scan)
**Shape:** Typed arg nodes; no C-text; interproc lattice.  
**Darwin:** Close 6 · Honest 4 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 0 → **avg 2.2 — REJECT**  
**Why dies:** Moonshot / DESIGN full taint. Out of residual 7.1.

### I8 — Naive `contains` / grep secret names on raw `args`
**Shape:** For each `__sec__*` name, `str` search in args.  
**Darwin:** Close 2 · Honest 0 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 6 → **avg 1.8 — DISQUALIFIED**  
**Why dies:** Guaranteed string/comment **FP**. Undoes T2-1/T2-2. Opposite of Path-A.

### I9 — Keep dual scan; document C-text as emit belt only
**Shape:** No code. `SECRET_TAINT.oot` already says this. Add one line to SPRINT 7.1 residual: “emit C-text belt; check is IDENT tokens.”  
**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 9 · Smoke 2 · Entropy 5 · Ship 9 → **avg 5.8**  
**Why not alone:** Honesty without prove. Ship **as a comment** inside I1+I5, not as the close.

### I10 — Shared **string-skip** walker only (no ident helper)
**Shape:** Extract `c_skip_c_quote` used by 7.1 + 7.2 last-arg + `c_count_top_args`.  
**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 8 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 6 · Ship 7 → **avg 6.0**  
**Why later hygiene:** Lowers copy-paste drift; does **not** close 7.1 or 7.10. Optional same-wave if line budget allows; not the CRIT.

