## Token-stream vs C-text (Decide card)

| | Token-stream (`c_secret_scan_call`) | C-text (`c_guard_scan_idents`) |
|--|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| Input | Lexer toks (`IDENT` field 3) | Lowered joined C `args` string |
| When | `check_secret_println_sinks` (check + emit-c + llvm) | `c_secret_emit_guard` after arg lower |
| String/comment FP | Impossible (not IDENT) | Possible if skip bugs; currently skips `"…"`, `//`, `/* */` |
| Heap | Token list already paid | O(\|args\|) char_at + **one slice / ident** (7.1 claim) |
| Path-A job | Source-faithful refuse | Belt if lower mangles / extra sealed sinks |
| 7.1 residual | Not the CRIT | **This is the CRIT** (was missing body + concat fear) |

**Ship-now decision:** keep **both**. Close 7.1 on the C-text walker’s **slice + skip prove**. Token unification = later (I3), not a substitute for I1.

## Top recommendation (this turn — path-A residual close)

### **Ship: Prove/close 7.1 (I1) + string/comment/alias smoke matrix (I5). Optionally land ident-slice helper (I4) on 7.10 same wave.**

**Why this closes 7.1:**
- Walker is already the Path-A fix (`str_slice`, no per-char OoStr). SPRINT “stack buffer” is a **wrong tool**.
- Unclosed part is **untested claim** (\(U\)): T2 fixtures for string/comment sit **unwired** to `secret_t2_depth_smoke.sh`.
- Alias resolve is already on the refuse path (`c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`); smoke must show dest-alias refuse, and must **name** callee-alias (`let f = println`) if emit C-text does not rewrite `t`.
- Shared helper is the right **7.10** close using the **7.1** pattern — not a 7.1 rewrite.

### DE winner advice (plain English)

1. **Do not rewrite** `c_guard_scan_idents` into tokens or a C `char[]`.
2. **Prove static:** in `c_emit_secret_guard.oo`, ident materialization is `str_slice` only.
3. **Wire smoke (I5):** extend `secret_t2_depth_smoke.sh` (preferred) **or** add `secret_s71_ident_scan_smoke.sh` called from `ci_product.sh`. Minimum new cases: `secret_t2_string_fp`, `secret_t2_string_lit_arg_fp`, `secret_t2_comment_fp`, `secret_t2_real_arg_fail`. Add alias: `secret_alias_rebind_pass` refuse. Dual-path check if cheap (T2 security already showed emit+check).
4. **SPRINT 7.1:** mark FIXED path-A **only after** smoke exit 0 on rebuilt host. Replace “stack buffer” wording.
5. **If same-wave budget:** I4 `c_ident_end` / `c_slice_ident_at` → rewrite **7.10** `c_parse_secret_env` name loop to one slice. Leave 7.2 last-arg as-is (already sliced; not an ident).
6. **Done bar:**
   - String/comment spelling of a SECRET name does **not** refuse.
   - Bare IDENT at sealed sink **does** refuse (`ERR\tsecret`).
   - Alias dest (`y = api_key; println(y)`) refuses.
   - Grep: no `name = name + c` inside `c_guard_scan_idents`.
   - Callee-alias / interp / IFC remain **named residual** (not silent OK).
7. **Out of scope:** I2 drop C-text; I3 emit tok plumbing; I6 C buffer; I7 lattice; I8 grep.

### Explicit non-winners (do not build this turn)

- C stack buffer / runtime C helper as the 7.1 “fix” (I6)  
- Delete C-text scan “because tokens exist” (I2)  
- Emit-guard signature rewrite to toks (I3)  
- Full IFC / AST lattice (I7)  
- Raw `contains` of secret names (I8)  
- M1–M20 moonshots  

## Entropy report (expected after winner)

`S: ↓` — 7.1 “FIXED in comments” → **smoke-proved** slice + FP/FN matrix; SPRINT wording debt cleared.  
`U` holds only for: token/C-text unification (I3), 7.10 until I4 lands, callee-alias completeness, `${}` (5.8).  
`O` does not rise (no second scanner architecture).

